SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] New MaineCare Partner Portal: Multi-Factor Au
 thentication (MFA) Requirements
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			New MaineCare Partner Portal: Multi-Factor Authenticati
 on (MFA) Requirements\nNew MaineCare Partner Portal: Multi-Factor Authenti
 cation (MFA) Requirements\nOct 06\, 2026\nAs a reminder\, the new MaineCar
 e Partner Portal is scheduled to go live on\nOctober 12\, 2026\, at 8:00 A
 M\n. The new portal will replace the current HealthPAS Online Portal and w
 ill require Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA). Read below for more informa
 tion and steps you will need to take to sign into the MaineCare Partner Po
 rtal\nstarting on October 12\n.\nFor all information about the upcoming ch
 anges to MIHMS\, see the “HealthPAS Online Portal” section of the\nPro
 vider Resources\npage.\nMulti-Factor Authenticator (MFA)\nMFA adds a secon
 d verification step after entering your password. This is an important new
  security measure to protect the sensitive information held in the Portal.
  You will have three options to choose from for your additional authentica
 tion factor\; you must choose one.\nFollow the instructions below for firs
 t-time setup of the option you choose.\nMicrosoft Authenticator\nThe Micro
 soft Authenticator app is the recommended MFA method because it offers the
  highest level of protection over other methods. Download the Microsoft Au
 thenticator app\nnow\non a smartphone or tablet so that you are ready to u
 se it on October 12.\nNo sooner than October 12\, follow these steps to se
 t up MFA via the app:\nTrading Partners with existing (migrated) Portal ac
 counts:\nOpen the Microsoft Authenticator app.\nClick “Sign In” on the
  MaineCare Partner Portal\; you will see a User Details window pop up.\nCl
 ick the QR code scanner in the Microsoft Authenticator app and scan the QR
  code displayed on the Portal’s User Details window.\nTrading Partners w
 ithout existing (new or non-migrated) Portal accounts\nwill set this up as
  part of the registration process.\nText/Call\nText (SMS) or call verifica
 tion \nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/new-mai
 necare-partner-portal-multi-factor-authentication-mfa-requirements-2026-10
 -06
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/new-mainec
 are-partner-portal-multi-factor-authentication-mfa-requirements-2026-10-06
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
