SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Board of Occupational Safety and Health to Ho
 st Listening Sessions on Proposed Indoor Air Quality Compliance Directive
DESCRIPTION:Skip First Level Navigation\nSkip All Navigation\nMaine.gov\nA
 gencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nMaine Departmen
 t of Labor\nContact Us\n|\nNews\n|\nOnline services\n|\nPublications\n|\nS
 itemap\nHome\nContact Us\nOnline Services\nAbout MDOL\nNews & Events\nForm
 s & Publications\nMDOL Bureaus\nHome\n→\nNews & Events\n→ Board of Occ
 upational Safety and Health to Host Listening Sessions on Proposed Indoor 
 Air Quality Compliance Directive\nServices\nJobs & Training\nUnemployment 
 Insurance\nDisability Services\nWorkplace Safety\nLabor Laws\nLabor Statis
 tics\nWorkforce Development\nBoard of Occupational Safety and Health to Ho
 st Listening Sessions on Proposed Indoor Air Quality Compliance Directive\
 nOctober 6\, 2026\nFor Immediate Release\nMedia Contact: Autumn Mahoney\, 
 Communications Specialist\nmedia.dol@maine.gov\nAUGUSTA - The Board of Occ
 upational Safety and Health (BOSH) and the Maine Department of Labor Burea
 u of Labor Standards (BLS) Workplace Safety and Health Division invite int
 erested parties and the public to participate in listening sessions on a\n
 proposed voluntary compliance directive on indoor air quality\n.\nBOSH reg
 ulates and enforces workplace safety and health rules that apply to public
  employers\, including state and local governmental agencies\, school dist
 ricts and quasi-governmental agencies. BOSH is considering publishing a vo
 luntary compliance directive to help public employers monitor and maintain
  healthy indoor air quality in public workplaces. The proposed compliance 
 directive is based in part on the research and recommendations of the Indo
 or Air Quality Advisory Group in 2025.\nBOSH and BLS will host the followi
 ng listening sessions:\nOct. 13\, 2026\, at 1 p.m. at the SafetyWorks! Tra
 ining Institute\, 45 Commerce Dr.\, Augusta\nNov. 2\, 2026\, at 3 p.m. by 
 Zoom with a focus on public school and education employers\nhttps://maines
 tate.zoom.us/j/82302635655?pwd=b1nVGHTd2yeypvjPXwaJlAkK2YhjkL.1\nNov. 9\, 
 2026\, at 10 a.m. by Zoom\nhttps://mainestate.zoom.us/j/89708408033?pwd=XN
 Ua0qqLPRc\nhttp://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=1336377
 6
URL:http://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13363776
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
