UID:65cded7d60052cde@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260930T221247Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] National PA Week - October 6 through 12
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, quality\, cost-effective\, and patient-centered he
 althcare is essential to the well-being and quality of life of all people 
 in Maine\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, physician associates/assistants (PAs) are nati
 onally certified and state-licensed medical professionals who diagnose ill
 nesses\, develop and manage treatment plans\, prescribe medications\, and 
 often serve as a patient's principal healthcare provider\; and\nWHEREAS\n\
 , PAs are trusted providers and vital members of the healthcare team\, enh
 ancing access to high-quality care in primary care settings\, hospitals\, 
 rural communities\, and underserved areas\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, PAs deliver c
 ompassionate\, expert care\, often serving as the first point of contact f
 or patients and empowering individuals and families to be active participa
 nts in their own health\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, PAs provide critical care acros
 s a broad range of medical specialties\, including addressing the growing 
 demand for behavioral and mental health services by offering compassionate
 \, evidence-based care to individuals and families in need\; and\nWHEREAS\
 n\, PAs are committed to addressing health disparities\, expanding access\
 , and providing team-based\, person-centered care across every medical spe
 cialty and setting\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, PAs have earned the respect of patie
 nts and colleagues alike for their clinical excellence\, adaptability\, an
 d deep dedication to the communities they serve\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine h
 as been a leader in progressing PA practice and ensuring access to PA serv
 ices by enacting legislation in recent years to join the PA compact\, chan
 ge the title of the profession to accurately reflect the scope of the prof
 ession\, and allow PAs to practice at the top of their education and train
 ing\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Govern
 or of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim October 6-12\, 2026 as\nNati
 onal PA Week\nin Maine\, and I encourage all residents to recognize and ce
 lebrate the important role that PAs play in improving health\, advancing e
 qui\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/
 2026-09-national-pa-week-october-6-through-12
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-09-national-pa-week-october-6-through-12
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9ca11fca84d79505@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260930T221247Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Domestic Violence Awareness Month - October
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\,\ndomestic abuse and violence is a serious injusti
 ce and public health crisis that affects people and families of all
  races\, ages\, genders\, sexual orientations\, and income levels\; 
 and\nWHEREAS\,\neach year nearly half of all homicides in Maine a
 re related to domestic abuse and violence\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nsupport an
 d help are available 24/7/365 to anyone affected by domestic abuse\, throu
 gh the programs of the Maine Coalition to End Domestic Violence and the st
 atewide domestic violence helpline\; and\nWHEREAS\,\ndomestic abuse and vi
 olence is entirely preventable\, and all Maine people have opportunities t
 o intervene and change the ways we and our communities understand and act 
 on the issue of domestic abuse and violence\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, community l
 eaders are uniquely positioned to make a broad and lasting impact by enact
 ing policies and practices that support survivors and their children\, and
  hold abusive people to account\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\,\nbe it resolved that
  I\, Janet T. Mills\,\nGovernor of the State of Maine\, do hereby pr
 oclaim October 2026 as\nDomestic Violence Awareness Month\nthroughout t
 he State of Maine\, and I urge all citizens to recognize this ob
 servance.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused\nthe Great Seal of the Sta
 te to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN under my\nhand at Augusta this twenty eig
 hth day of\nSeptember Two Thousand Twenty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/govern
 or/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2026-09-domestic-violence-awaren
 ess-month-october
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-09-domestic-violence-awareness-month-october
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5a55f34031a88355@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260930T221247Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Disability Employment Awareness Month - Octob
 er
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, October 2026 marks the 81st anniversary of Nationa
 l Disability Employment Awareness Month\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, workplaces acro
 ss our state that are welcoming of the talents of all people\, including p
 eople with disabilities\, are critical to healthy communities and a strong
  economy\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, while the employment rate of people with disab
 ilities ages 16 to 64 in Maine has increased to 44 percent\, it remains si
 gnificantly lower than the 83 percent employment rate for Maine people wit
 hout disabilities\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, it is important that the State of Mai
 ne prepare all youth\, including those with disabilities\, for meaningful 
 careers and an adulthood that includes employment\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine
  is an Employment First state\, affirming employment as the first and pref
 erred option for people with disabilities who receive services from state 
 agencies\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, people with disabilities\, including people wh
 o are Deaf\, Hard of Hearing\, Late Deafened\, Blind or with Low Vision ma
 ke significant contributions to Maine's economy and communities\; and\nWHE
 REAS\n\, activities during this month will reinforce the value and talent 
 people with disabilities add to our workplaces and communities and affirm 
 Maine's commitment to increasing access to good jobs and competitive\, int
 egrated employment for all workers\, including those with disabilities\;\n
 NOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of t
 he State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim October 2026 as\nDisability Employm
 ent Awareness Month\nthroughout the State of Maine\, and I call upon emplo
 yers\, schools\, higher education institutions and other community organiz
 ations in Maine to observe October with appropriate programs and activitie
 s that celebrate the contributions of people with disabilities and promote
  access to good\, in-demand jobs and career pathways such as registered ap
 prenticeships for all Maine people.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused\
 nthe Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN under my\nha\nh
 ttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2026-0
 9-disability-employment-awareness-month-october
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-09-disability-employment-awareness-month-october
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
